VANGERS: One for the Road
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

1. Required libraries:

   - SDL 3.2 or newer
   - SDL_net 3.2 or newer
   - libvorbis
   - SDL3-native clunk from the upstream `master` branch
     (https://github.com/stalkerg/clunk)
   - ffmpeg 6.0 or newer
   - toml11 4.4.x
   - zlib

2. Required tools:

   - CMake 4.0 or newer
   - Ninja or make

3. Building:

   $ mkdir build
   $ cd build
   $ cmake ..
   $ make

4. Running:

   $ cd data
   $ ../build/src/vangers


Windows (MSYS2) helper scripts

The OSS Windows build can be reproduced locally with the scripts in
packaging/msys2. They mirror the "OSS Windows 64bit Build" GitHub Actions job
and are split into three steps:

   > powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File packaging\msys2\install-msys2.ps1
   > powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File packaging\msys2\build-msys2.ps1
   > powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File packaging\msys2\run-msys2.ps1 <game-dir>

install-msys2.ps1 installs MSYS2 automatically (into C:\msys64 by default) when
it is not present, updates it, and installs the required packages plus the pinned
clunk and toml11; use -Msys2Root, -NoInstallMsys2, -ClunkRepo, -ClunkCommit,
-Msys2Version, -Msys2InstallerUrl, -Msys2Sha256 and -NoUpdate to override the
defaults. build-msys2.ps1 only configures, builds and tests Vangers (use
-BuildType, -BuildDir and -SkipTests). run-msys2.ps1 copies the built binaries and
their MSYS2 runtime DLLs into <game-dir> and launches the game (add -NoRun to copy
only).

The underlying .sh scripts can also be run directly from an MSYS2 UCRT64 shell.
install-msys2.sh requires a completed full update: either run it as
`MSYS2_UPDATED=1 ./packaging/msys2/install-msys2.sh` after updating manually
(pacman -Syu, reopening the terminal if it updated msys2-runtime, then pacman -Syu
again), or use the PowerShell entry point, which drives the restart.


OSX prerequisites

a. Install homebrew
b. brew install sdl3 sdl3_net libvorbis libogg ffmpeg toml11
c. Build/install the upstream `master` branch of clunk
   (https://github.com/stalkerg/clunk).
d. Go to 3.


Android integration

The Android host project must provide native SDL3 and SDL3_net CMake packages,
for example through their official Prefab-enabled Android archives, and an
SDL3-native Clunk build. With `ANDROID` enabled this repository builds the
static `vangers` library and exports the standard SDL3 `SDL_main()` entry point
for the host activity's native entry point. The host build must also provide a
toml11 4.4.x CMake package. Save-game files keep their existing binary format.
User preferences migrate once from `options.dat` and `controls.dat` to
`settings.toml`; the legacy files are left unchanged.
